<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15609" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρτηρία</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ιη,</span>
		ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>wind-pipe,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ἀ. μόλις ἀναπνεούσῃ ὑπεσύριζε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Epid.</u>
					7.25
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				39
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				70d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				493a8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>de An.</u>
				420b29
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡτραχεῖα ἀ.</span> (cf. <i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>) Timoth. ap. Meno.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Iatr.</u>
				8.29
			</span></i>, v. l. in <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				2.50
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Hist. Conscr.</u>
				7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>M.</u>
				9.178
			</span></i>, etc.: in pl., <i>bronchial tubes,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἆσθμα . . περὶ στήθεα καὶ ἀρτηρίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Epid.</u>
					7.12
				</span></i>
			 (vulg. but prob. l. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ίην,</span>
			=
			<i>trachea</i>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				78c
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλεύμονος ἀρτηρίαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					1054
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>artery,</i> as distinct from a vein, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ φλεβῶν καὶ ἀρτηριῶν κοινωνίαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Art.</u>
					45
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				69
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς δὲ φλέβας καὶ τὰς ἀ. συνάπτειν
					εἰς ἀλλήλας . . τῇ αἰσθήσει φανερὸν εἶναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Spir.</u>
					484a1
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. λεῖαι</span> (cf. I) <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				<u>UP</u>
				8.1
			</span></i>, al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. φλεβώδης</span>
			<i>pulmonary vein,</i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				6.10
			</span></i>; believed to contain <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πνεῦμα</span>
			by <i><span class="en">
				Erasistr.
			</span></i>, ib. <i><span class="en">
				17
			</span></i>, and derived fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀήρ,
			τηρέω</span> by <i><span class="en">
				Bacch.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Erot.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀορτέων.</span>
			
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀορτή</span>
			, <i>aorta,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δύο εἰσὶ κοῖλαι φλέβες ἀπὸ τῆς
					καρδίης, τῇ μὲν οὔνομα ἀρτηρίη τῇ δὲ κοίλη φλέψ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Carn.</u>
					5
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b> in pl. of the
				<i>ureters,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Oss.</u>
				10
			</span></i>. (Contr. from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀερτηρία,</span>
			from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀείρω</span> 'attach' (q. v.), cf.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀορτήρ,</span> etc.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
